From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Pearson <tpearson@raptorengineering.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:33:59 +1100
Subject: feat: enable the seccomp-bpf sandbox on ppc64

Add the ppc64 syscall tables, ucontext accessors and policy tweaks the
Linux sandbox needs to run renderers under seccomp-bpf on ppc64le.

Origin: Debian chromium packaging, debian/patches/ppc64le/sandbox/0001-sandbox-Enable-seccomp_bpf-for-ppc64.patch (156.0.8078.79-1).

diff --git a/sandbox/features.gni b/sandbox/features.gni
index 8c5db2c6fa6cf772a1329be016ba00a82e4d69e4..1312860c77d58ac9335204314404bdfa46e0b32b 100644
--- a/sandbox/features.gni
+++ b/sandbox/features.gni
@@ -9,4 +9,5 @@
 use_seccomp_bpf = (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android) &&
                   (current_cpu == "x86" || current_cpu == "x64" ||
                    current_cpu == "arm" || current_cpu == "arm64" ||
-                   current_cpu == "mipsel" || current_cpu == "mips64el")
+                   current_cpu == "mipsel" || current_cpu == "mips64el" ||
